<ProbModelXML formatVersion="1.0.0">
  <ProbNet type="DAN">
    <Comment showWhenOpeningNetwork="true"><![CDATA[<html>
  <head>
    
  </head>
  <body>
    <p style="margin-top: 0">
      In this problem, if we order the test now, its result will be known 
      tomorrow. Therefore, the first variable, <i>Do test?</i>, reveals <i>Result 
      of test</i> but not immediately; when making the second decision, <i>Therapy 
      today</i>, the <i>Result of test</i> is still unknown. For this reason, 
      we have added a revelation arc from the second decision to <i>Result of 
      test</i>. Similarly, <i>Symptom tomorrow</i> is observed spontaneously, 
      but only after the first two decisions have been made. For this reason, 
      we have added a revelation arc from the second decision to <i>Symptom 
      tomorrow</i>. A more elegant solution would be to use a multi-stage DAN; 
      the &quot;tomorrow&quot; variables, including <i>Result of test</i>, 
      would be placed in the second stage. <i>Symptom tomorrow</i> would be 
      marked as <i>Always observed</i>, but it will be known only for the 
      decisions in the second and posterior stages.
    </p>
  </body>
</html>]]></Comment>
    <DecisionCriteria>
